<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Syllabus Template</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  th, td {
    padding: 8px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .centered {
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 18pt;">US AGRICULTURAL LAW</h1>
    <h2 style="font-size: 14pt;">AGEC 342 – FALL {{ current_year }}</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 12pt;">School of Agriculture – Western Illinois University</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">INSTRUCTOR</h3>
      <p>Dr. <span data-field="instructor.last_name">{{ instructor.last_name }}</span> <span data-field="instructor.first_name">{{ instructor.first_name }}</span></p>
      <p>Ag Office Phone: <span data-field="instructor.office_phone">{{ instructor.office_phone }}</span></p>
      <p>Office Fax: <span data-field="instructor.office_fax">{{ instructor.office_fax }}</span></p>
      <p>E-mail: <span data-field="instructor.email">{{ instructor.email }}</span></p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">Office</h3>
      <p>Office: <span data-field="office.location">{{ office.location }}</span></p>
      <p>Office Hours: M, T, W, Th 8:00-9:00 by email or other electronic method as needed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">CLASS TIMES AND LOCATIONS</h3>
    <p>AGEC 342 is an online course found at <a href="http://www.westernonline.wiu.edu">{{ course_url }}</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">EMAILS</h3>
    <p>Please be sure to include the course in which you are enrolled in any emails.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">COURSE DESCRIPTION AND PREREQUISITES</h3>
    <p>Law as it applies to the agricultural operation. Partnership, corporation, agribusiness contracts, leases, leasing practices, environmental, tort and liability law are covered.</p>
    <p>Prerequisite: AGRI 220. 3 hrs. lect.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">TEXTS AND OTHER MATERIAL</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Recommended: <span data-field="textbook.title">{{ textbook.title }}</span>, <span data-field="textbook.author">{{ textbook.author }}</span>, <span data-field="textbook.edition">{{ textbook.edition }}</span>, ISBN <span data-field="textbook.isbn">{{ textbook.isbn }}</span>.</li>
      <li>Supplemental Handouts</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">COURSE OBJECTIVES</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>To develop a basic understanding of law and the legal system as it pertains to agriculture.</li>
      <li>To learn basic legal terminology relevant to duty, liability, contracts, tenancy, property transfer, and organization and operation of businesses.</li>
      <li>To gain practical experience regarding civil and criminal procedures through mock trials.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">EXPECTATIONS OF STUDENTS</h3>
    <p>Participation: Students are expected to regularly attend class and to actively participate in discussions.</p>
    <p>Online Absence Reporting System (OARS) - <a href="{{ oars_link }}">http://wiu.edu/oars</a>.</p>
    <p>Academic Integrity: The rules and regulations outlined in the University's policy on academic integrity are applied to this course. See <a href="{{ integrity_link }}">http://www.wiu.edu/policies/acintegirty.php</a>.</p>
    <p>Disruptive Student Behavior: Behave yourself. <a href="{{ behavior_link }}">http://www.wiu.edu/vpas/policies/disrupt.php</a>.</p>
    <p>Student Rights and Responsibilities: Detailed information regarding student rights and responsibilities can be found at <a href="{{ rights_link }}">http://www.wiu.edu/provost/student/</a>. It is your responsibility to be familiar with the posted information.</p>
    <p>Special Accommodations: If you need special accommodations, please feel free to stop by and discuss your needs or contact Disability Resource Center at 309-298-2512 or <span data-field="disability_email">{{ disability_email }}</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">TOBACCO POLICY</h3>
    <p>Tobacco use of any kind will not be tolerated in class. This includes chewing tobacco.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">USE OF CELLULAR PHONES</h3>
      <p>As a courtesy to other students and to the instructor, all cell phones should be turned off prior to class. Continued disregard of this policy may result in ejection from the course. If, due to medical or public safety concerns, a student needs an exception to this policy he/she should inform the instructor prior to class. Cell phones are not to be used under any circumstances on exams. Texting is not allowed during class and repeated violations may lead to dismissal from the course with an assigned grade of F.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 50%;">
      <h3 class="section-title">IMPORTANT DATES</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th style="width: 30%;">Date</th>
            <th style="width: 70%;">Event</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Sep 4</td>
            <td>Last day to drop without being assessed tuition or receiving a "W" grade</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Sep 7</td>
            <td>Labor Day: No Class</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Oct 2</td>
            <td>Fall Break: No Class</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Nov 1</td>
            <td>Last day to drop with a "W"</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Dec 14</td>
            <td>Comprehensive Final Exam: 1:00 pm – 2:50 pm</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">GRADING POLICY</h3>
    <p>The course grade will be based on the following factors, with weightings as indicated:</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 30%;">Assessment</th>
          <th style="width: 20%;">Weight</th>
          <th style="width: 50%;">Grading Scale</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Quizzes</td>
          <td>20%</td>
          <td>A = 93% or above, C- = 70-72.99%</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Discussion Boards</td>
          <td>20%</td>
          <td>A- = 90-92.99%, D+ = 67-69.99%</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Midterm Exam</td>
          <td>30%</td>
          <td>B+ = 87-89.99%, D = 63-66.99%</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Comprehensive Final Exam</td>
          <td>30%</td>
          <td>B = 83-86.99%, D- = 60-62.99%</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Total</td>
          <td>100%</td>
          <td>B = 80-82.99%, F = &lt;60%</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Grade breaking points may be lowered, but in no case will they be raised. These breaking points will be evaluated only after final numerical grades have been calculated.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">Attention Education Majors:</h3>
    <p>The changes within the state teaching license require all education majors to receive a grade of a "C-" or better in this course in order to meet Illinois teaching license requirements. With the university +/- grading system, receiving a "D+" or below will require you to retake this course or find a substitute course to meet School of Agriculture graduation requirements.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">QUIZZES/HOMEWORK</h3>
    <p>Quizzes are on Western Online, remain open for the semester, and may be retaken an unlimited number of times for the highest score. Posts in mock trial discussion boards and are due at 11:59 p.m. Sunday at the end of the specified workweek.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">EXAMS</h3>
    <p>There will be one midterm and one comprehensive final exam. Exams will consist of true/false and multiple-choice questions. Exams are limited to one attempt, so make sure you are using a reliable internet connection when attempting the exams. Makeup exams will only be given in extreme situations.</p>
    <p>If a student disagrees with a particular answer, it is the student's responsibility to provide a logical reason in writing as to the reason for disagreement. This does not apply to scoring errors. All instructors are human and occasional errors in grading will occur. Bring any such errors to the instructor's attention immediately.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">COURSE OUTLINE</h3>
    <p>Students will review slides (Powerpoint) notes and complete corresponding quizzes. The primary lectures are listed in the outline below, and supplemental lectures and other materials are available on Western Online for students interested in additional review or further exploration of topics. Discussion board assignments and exams are bolded in the outline below, "-->" denotes that the quiz will open once the student comments on the discussion board for the associated mock trial. Quizzes will remain open for the semester, and may be retaken an unlimited number of times for the highest score. There will also be one shot each at a midterm and a comprehensive final exam, so make sure you are using a reliable internet connection when attempting the exams.</p>
  </div>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 10%;">Week</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">Start of Week</th>
        <th style="width: 75%;">Topic/Material</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for week in course_outline %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ loop.index }}</td>
        <td>{{ week.start_date }}</td>
        <td>{{ week.topic }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">ACCREDITATION</h3>
    <p>The School of Agriculture is housed in the College of Business and Technology which is accredited by AACSB-International.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h3 class="section-title">NOTICES</h3>
    <p>Please be advised that this syllabus is tentative. All classes are different and we may or may not be able to address all of the content areas or stick with the anticipated number of exams. Any deviations from the syllabus will be announced as soon as possible.</p>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>